cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "VRFS: Video Recompression Forensics Suite"
abstract: >-
  VRFS detects double compression in H.264 video from three independent
  evidence axes: the quantization-step comb in the AC coefficient histogram,
  the phase of the frame-size series, and the distortion residual in the pixel
  domain. An applicability gate runs before any verdict and the result is
  reported as a 0-100 evidence-strength score together with three verdicts,
  including a distinct not-applicable outcome.
version: 1.0.0
date-released: "2026-10-12"
license: MIT
type: software
repository-code: "https://github.com/adhoccn/video-recompression-forensics"
url: "https://github.com/adhoccn/video-recompression-forensics"
keywords:
  - video forensics
  - double compression
  - H.264
  - multimedia forensics
  - completely monotone
  - quantization step
  - GOP structure
authors:
  - name: "VRFS Contributors"
